CORE
descending_init_512.sv
--top main --bound 3
^\[main\.p_low\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_high\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_rt\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_rt_value\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_write\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.r_sanity\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
512 descending words initialised one by one, as Yosys writes a memory with
an init file. A constant index is one element; as a selector over all 512
elements per initial word, this took 13 seconds and 1.1 GB.
